# L §4.5 Whatever a version states is read as its rows are (tally 2.1.8 R12, #169-j; T's fixes/g6b/b4_q1q3): a version's
# same line is seen under a cut only when known by it. sm (known 2026-03-02) joins x and y: unseen as known 2026-01-01
# and 2026-03-01, so x is 3 and y is 4 (q1, q3); seen at on, the two rows disagree, HOLE-SAME (q2). 2.1.7's refcore
# read the line at every cut and printed HOLE-SAME for q1 and q3.
=== m.tally
model p
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input x: int
input y: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x = 3 "s"
  y = 4 "s"

ask q1: x as known 2026-01-01
ask q2: x
ask q3: y as known 2026-03-01

version sm
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-03-02
  same x = y
=== expect
q1: 3
  cut 2026-01-01
q2: ?"x and y are one, but the value differs on every day: 3 (v:x) and 4 (v:y)" (x, y)
  cut 2026-06-30
q3: 4
  cut 2026-03-01
